{"status":"confirmed","reasoning":"I is false: tangent has vertical asymptotes at x=\pi/2+n\pi, while x=n\pi gives zeros. II is true because tangent has period \pi, so adding 2n\pi preserves its value wherever defined. III is false because tangent's range is all real numbers. Thus "II only", current option "0", agrees with the earlier answer and the captured solution's three truth judgments.","confidence":1,"answers":[{"key":"selection","correct_value":"II only","correct_option":"0","value_type":"text","wrong_value":"III only","correct_keys":[],"wrong_keys":[],"ma_value":"II only","ma_basis":"worked_solution","ma_evidence":"Verbatim: "- Statement I is false. The function $y=tan⁡x$ has asymptotes at $x=\frac{\pi }{2}+\pi n.$

- Statement II is true. The function has period $\pi .$ So, $tan⁡(x+2n\pi )=tan⁡(x+n\pi +n\pi )=tan⁡(x+n\pi )=tan⁡(x).$

- Statement III is false. The range of $y=tan⁡x$ is $(-\infty ,+\infty ).$"","disagrees":false}]}
